# The environment this reader needs on Vercel.

# Nothing here is secret. Every value is a public network endpoint or a display name,
# and every one of them already has a default in the source, so a deployment with no
# variables set at all will build and run against Studionet. They are listed because a
# deployment that silently uses a default is a deployment nobody has looked at.
#
# There is no private key, and there must never be one. The reader holds no key and
# signs nothing; the keeper key used by `scripts/` and `deploy/deployScript.ts` stays on
# whatever machine runs them. If a variable starting with DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY or
# FIDE_KEY_FILE ever appears in this file's usage, it is being wired into the reader
# wrongly — the deploy scripts run on a developer's machine, not in a web deployment.

# Which trust the landing page features. Overrides the first entry in the registry.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURED_TRUST=0x76051A36dCB316bD7Bf272692B3e3f7930170597

# The JSON-RPC endpoint. A browser-like User-Agent is required or Cloudflare answers with
# error 1010, so this must be reached from the server, which is what lib/genlayer.ts does.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GENLAYER_RPC_URL=https://studio.genlayer.com/api

# Shown in the reader's chrome and in the wallet's chain entry.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GENLAYER_CHAIN_NAME=GenLayer Studio
NEXT_PUBLIC_GENLAYER_SYMBOL=GEN

# The block explorer is NOT configurable. It is a constant in lib/explorer.ts, and the
# reader's links and the wallet's chain entry both read that one constant, so they
# cannot point at different explorers. Setting NEXT_PUBLIC_EXPLORER_URL would do nothing;
# it was removed when the wallet stopped defaulting to an empty list.